      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the vCPU has been already created successfully, it means `postponed_per_vm_setup()` already succeeded during the first vCPU creation (with valid values of irqchip_mode and max_vcpu_ids), so during creation of subsequent vCPUs, pKVM will not call `postponed_per_vm_setup()` anymore, i.e. it will not even try to use those new possibly invalid values of irqchip_mode and max_vcpu_ids, it will use the same (valid) values as for the first vCPU, right?",
      "parentUuid": "10b73bf5_4ecb8cb8",
      "revId": "8acdd620e71eaff4ec0c5ca2f3aa54ec0f529482",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
